<title>USA: White House aide Lindsey monitors tobacco talks.</title>
<headline>White House aide Lindsey monitors tobacco talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Presidential aide Bruce Lindsey, who was to leave with President Bill Clinton for the G7 summit in Denver, remained in Washington to monitor tobacco settlement talks, the White House said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Lindsey, who has been in regular contact with both sides throughout the negotiations, &quot;is staying here,&quot; Press Secretary Mike McCurry said, moments before Clinton departed the White House for the summit. McCurry said Lindsey planned to leave for Denver on Saturday.</p>
</text>
